{"name":"Afternoon Stroll","hex":"#d9c5a1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"afternoon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the day from noon or lunchtime until sunset, evening, or suppertime or 6pm.","The later part of anything, often with implications of decline."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In the afternoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon"},{"term":"stroll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wandering on foot; an idle and leisurely walk; a ramble; a saunter.","A dance of the 1950s in which dancers leisurely stepped, cross-stepped, and dipped at the knee to the beat of the music."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wander on foot; to ramble idly or leisurely; to rove.","To go somewhere with ease."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroll"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afternoon","blocks":[{"text":"Afternoon is the period from noon to sunset or evening. It is the time when the sun is descending from its peak in the sky to somewhat before its terminus at the horizon in the west. In human life, it occupies roughly the latter half of the standard work and school day. In literal terms, it refers to a time specifically after noon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg/330px-Wien_T%C3%BCrkenschanzpark_%282376611600%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afternoon","wikidata":"Q283102"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_Of_Art_%285894065780%29.jpg/1280px-Rooftop_Bar%2C_Metropolitan_